    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. \n\nWater absorption in the small intestine primarily occurs via the paracellular pathway, where water moves between enterocytes through tight junctions following the osmotic gradient created by solute transport (specifically sodium). While transcellular transport via aquaporins exists, the majority of intestinal water absorption is paracellular. Other options are incorrect because they mischaracterize the primary transport mechanism or the fluid balance dynamics of the gut.",
