    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Improved marginal adaptation in a composite restoration is enhanced by ensuring a clean, dry field and proper bonding, which is facilitated by an acid-etching technique that increases surface area and promotes micromechanical retention. Acid etching removes the smear layer and opens up porosities in the enamel, allowing better resin tag formation and marginal seal. Although a moisture-free environment and pressure application are important, acid etching is the most critical factor directly influencing marginal adaptation.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
