    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The sonic frequency range typically refers to the range of human hearing, which is generally from 20 Hz to 20,000 Hz (20 kHz). Among the given options, the only one that falls within or near the upper limit of this range is 20,000–30,000 Hz, but this exceeds the normal human hearing range. However, since the question might be misworded or referring to ultrasonic ranges, none of the options perfectly represent the typical sonic (audible) range. Still, the closest standard reference for high-frequency hearing is up to 20,000 Hz, making D (10,000 Hz) too low, and C too high. But if interpreting \"sonic\" as \"audible,\" then none are correct—however, **B** (1500–6000 Hz) represents the range of greatest human hearing sensitivity, particularly for speech.\n\nThus, the best answer based on context and typical interpretation is:\n\n\\boxed{B}",
