    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The transport of CO is diffusion limited because\n\nOptions: \nA. Binds avidly with Hb\nB. Partial pressure of CO is less\nC. CO is less absorbed in water\nD. Alveolar membrane is less permeable\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}.\n\nCarbon monoxide (CO) transport is diffusion-limited because it binds to hemoglobin with an affinity approximately 210 times greater than that of oxygen, which keeps the partial pressure of CO in the blood near zero. As a result, the concentration gradient for CO from the alveoli to the blood remains steep throughout the entire duration of capillary transit. Therefore, the total amount of CO transferred depends on the diffusing capacity of the alveolar-capillary membrane rather than the blood flow.",
