      "generated_answer": "The bicarbonate buffer system is considered the best buffer in the body primarily because its components can be independently regulated: CO₂ levels via respiration and HCO₃⁻ via renal function. This open-system flexibility allows rapid adjustments to maintain pH, unlike closed buffers with fixed concentrations. Options A, C, and D describe general buffer properties but do not capture the unique physiological advantage.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
