      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is A, as mean and standard deviation require numerical data with meaningful intervals and a true or arbitrary zero point, which is only found on interval or ratio scales.  \nDichotomous scales have only two categories, nominal scales involve unordered labels, and ordinal scales provide ranks without equal spacing — none allow for these calculations properly.  \nThus, mean and standard deviation are appropriate only for interval or ratio data.  \n\n\\boxed{A}",
