    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Enzymes function by lowering the activation energy of a chemical reaction, which allows more substrate molecules to reach the transition state at a given temperature, thereby increasing the reaction rate. While temperature increases can boost activity up to an optimal point, extreme heat or pH values typically denature enzymes, and low substrate concentration limits the activity. Therefore, the decrease of activation energy is the fundamental mechanism that facilitates increased catalytic activity.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
