    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Phenylbutyrate acts as a nitrogen-scavenging agent by being converted into phenylacetate, which then conjugates with glutamine to form phenylacetylglutamine. This conjugate is excreted by the kidneys, effectively removing excess waste nitrogen from the body and bypassing defective urea cycle enzymes. Therefore, it compensates for the metabolic block by providing an alternative pathway for nitrogen excretion.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
