    "global index": "MedMCQA_554",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A drug X was given continuous intravenous infusion at 1.6 mg/min. The clearance of the drug is 640 mL/min. With a half-life of 1.8 hours, what would be the steady state plasma concentration of drug?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.002 mg/mL\nB. 0.004 trig/mL\nC. 2.88 mg/mL\nD. 3.55 mg/mL\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To calculate the steady-state plasma concentration ($C_{ss}$), use the formula $C_{ss} = \\text{Rate of infusion} / \\text{Clearance}$. Given an infusion rate of 1.6 mg/min and a clearance of 640 mL/min, $C_{ss} = 1.6 / 640 = 0.0025$ mg/mL. Since 0.0025 is closest to the provided option A given potential rounding in clinical calculations, it is the most likely correct choice.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 162,
        "output_tokens": 125,
        "total_tokens": 287
