      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}\n\nYes, mitochondria play a role in remodelling lace plant leaves during programmed cell death. The study shows that mitochondrial dynamics change progressively during PCD stages, and inhibition of PTP formation with cyclosporine A reduced perforation formation. These findings indicate mitochondrial involvement in developmental PCD in lace plants.",
