      "generated_answer": "The study found that 71.2% of late post-tonsillectomy hemorrhages occurred during the night-time (between 9.00 p.m. and 9.00 a.m.), compared to 28.8% during the day-time, and this difference was statistically significant (p=0.002). This indicates a clear predominance of hemorrhages occurring at night. Therefore, late post-tonsillectomy hemorrhage is a preferably night-time event.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
