      "generated_answer": "The study shows that adding tranexamic acid to desmopressin significantly reduced postoperative drainage, blood product transfusions, and markers of fibrinolysis (such as fibrin split products) compared to desmopressin alone. Lower fibrin split products and higher fibrinogen levels in the tranexamic acid group indicate reduced fibrinolytic activity. Therefore, tranexamic acid effectively reduces desmopressin-induced hyperfibrinolysis.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
