      "generated_answer": "The study found that while overall Ki-67 values did not significantly differ across response groups (pCR, partial, stable/progressive disease), Ki-67 levels varied significantly among molecular subtypes and were significantly different between patients with and without pCR within the luminal group. This suggests a predictive role for Ki-67 in certain subtypes of breast cancer. Therefore, Ki-67 can play a role in predicting response to neoadjuvant chemotherapy, particularly in luminal tumors.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
