      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}\n\nYes, it is possible to stop treatment with nucleos(t)ide analogs in selected patients with HBeAg-negative chronic hepatitis B. Recent evidence and the study results show that while virological relapse occurs in many patients (54.54% in this study), a significant proportion remain in remission after discontinuation. Careful patient selection—such as those with sustained viral suppression, normal liver enzymes, and no cirrhosis—makes treatment discontinuation feasible.",
