    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Neo-Riemannian triadic theory, which transformation can convert the A major triad into an a minor triad?\n\nOptions: \nA. P transformation\nB. R transformation\nC. L transformation\nD. T transformation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The P (parallel) transformation directly converts a major triad to its parallel minor by lowering the third, which is exactly what is needed to change A major (A-C#-E) to A minor (A-C-E). The R transformation relates relative major and minor (e.g., C major to A minor), while L involves a leading-tone exchange (e.g., C major to E minor). Thus, the correct choice is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
