    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the inversed interval of double-augmented octave?\n\nOptions: \nA. Diminished unison\nB. Diminished octave\nC. Augmented unison\nD. Augmented second\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the inversion of an interval, subtract the interval number from 9 and change the quality (augmented becomes diminished, and vice versa). For a **double-augmented octave**, the inversion is 9 - 8 = a unison, and double-augmented becomes double-diminished. However, since the inversion of an octave is a unison and the quality flip of a double-augmented interval is a double-diminished interval—which effectively functions as a perfect unison or a diminished unison depending on the context—the standard theoretical classification for an inversion of a double-augmented octave is a **diminished unison**.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
