    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Opportunistic foraging is characterized by a flexible strategy where an individual or group consumes whatever resources are readily available in their immediate environment without extensive preparation or specialization. This approach stands in contrast to planned or logistical strategies, as it relies on responding to immediate encounters rather than scheduled harvests or long-term food storage. Therefore, it is defined by a lack of rigorous, long-term planning.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
