      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The passage explicitly states, \"we possess all things\" and the emperor has \"no use for your country's manufactures,\" indicating that China’s self-sufficiency led them to believe they had no need for British trade goods. This highlights the Qing dynasty's stance of economic independence at the time.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 372,
