      "generated_answer": "The provided text emphasizes the \"absolute necessity of uniting all our councils and all our strength\" to defend common liberties, highlighting the inherent weakness of a system that struggled to harmonize the disparate interests and resources of sovereign states. Historically, the Articles of Confederation were primarily hindered by a central government that lacked the authority to tax the states or regulate commerce effectively, making it nearly impossible to fund national operations. Therefore, the most accurate answer regarding the systemic weaknesses described in the context of the era's difficulties is the inability to raise necessary revenue.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
