    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4654",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n\"The question as to who, and what, is responsible for African underdevelopment can be answered at two levels. Firstly, the answer is that the operation of the imperialist system bears major responsibility for African economic retardation by draining African wealth and by making it impossible to develop more rapidly the resources of the continent. Secondly, one has to deal with those who manipulate the system and those who are either agents or unwitting accomplices of the said system. The capitalists of Western Europe were the ones who actively extended their exploitation from inside Europe to cover the whole of Africa.\"\nWalter Rodney, historian, How Europe Underdeveloped Africa, 1974\nWhich of the following best explains the importance of trading contacts with Europeans for Sub-Saharan Africans in the period 1450 to 1750 C.E.?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sub-Saharan Africans consolidated new states and kingdoms by trading with the Europeans for firearms.\nB. Sub-Saharan Africans relied on trading contacts with Europeans to circumvent the Arab slave trade.\nC. Sub-Saharan Africans depended on European merchants as the sole purchasers of slaves.\nD. Sub-Saharan Africans established significant economic advantage by trading indigenous resources for European goods.\nE. Sub-Saharan Africans developed a dependency on European goods, leading to a collapse of local industries.\nF. Sub-Saharan Africans used European trading contacts to gain access to European education and religion.\nG. Sub-Saharan Africans relied on European merchants to sustain population growth through the constant importation of New World foodstuffs.\nH. Sub-Saharan Africans allied with European powers to evict Muslim and Arab merchant princes from encroaching on their sovereignty.\nI. Sub-Saharan Africans utilized trading contacts with Europeans to spread their cultural influence throughout Europe.\nJ. Sub-Saharan Africans engaged in trade with Europeans to acquire new agricultural techniques.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}.\n\nDuring the period 1450 to 1750 C.E., many Sub-Saharan African states—such as the Asante Empire and the Kingdom of Dahomey—leveraged European trade, particularly the exchange of slaves and gold for firearms, to expand their military power and consolidate territorial control. This process fundamentally altered political power structures in coastal and interior regions, allowing some states to dominate their neighbors. Other options are historically inaccurate or do not capture the primary political impact of the era described.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 445,
        "output_tokens": 111,
        "total_tokens": 556
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
