      "generated_answer": "The Carlsbad Resolutions were reactionary measures championed by Prince Klemens von Metternich to suppress liberal and nationalist sentiment in the German states. Because these decrees were designed to censor the press and stifle political opposition to the conservative order, the liberals of the time would have naturally aligned with figures who advocated for political reform, nationalism, or individual rights. Among the choices, Giuseppe Mazzini—an Italian nationalist and revolutionary—shared the struggle against the conservative, anti-liberal status quo enforced by these decrees.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
