    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4754",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\nOh, shame on you, poor Winter King!\nWhat's this that you have done?\nIs 't not a very naughty thing\nTo snatch the kaiser's crown?\nNow you will have to stay away\nAlike from Rhine and Prague,\nAnd more than that-shame and dismay\nYour days and nights will plague.\nRight well you knew, and all the world,\nRight well they know this thing,\nThat Ferdinand alone can be\nBohemia's lawful king.\nSo come, dear Fritz, rouse up and go\nTo Ferdinand, your king,\nAnd beg him graciously to show\nFull pardon for your sin.\n\"Poor Winter King,\" seventeenth-century song\nThe narrator of the song would most likely identify as which of the following?\n\nOptions: \nA. Roman Catholic\nB. Muslim\nC. Agnostic\nD. Hindu\nE. Atheist\nF. Eastern Orthodox\nG. Buddhist\nH. Sikh\nI. Protestant\nJ. Jewish\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The song refers to the \"Winter King\" (Frederick V, Elector Palatine) and his unsuccessful seizure of the Bohemian throne, which was a central catalyst for the Thirty Years' War between Catholic and Protestant forces. The narrator expresses strong support for the legitimacy of Ferdinand II, the Catholic Holy Roman Emperor, and portrays Frederick's actions as a sinful rebellion. Given this historical context and the monarchist viewpoint, the narrator most likely identifies as a Catholic.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
