      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}.\n\nThe letters illustrate that both parties recognized a high volume of trade, with King Afonso noting the \"voracious appetite\" of his people for European goods and King Manuel emphasizing the need for ships to be filled with slaves, copper, or ivory. While King Afonso expresses grievances regarding the kidnapping of his people, the documents confirm a mutually active, albeit exploitative, commercial relationship.",
