    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    N, M = map(int, input().split())\n    S = input().strip()\n    \n    plain_tshirts = M\n    logo_tshirts = 0  # initially 0, we will calculate how many we need to buy\n    current_plain = M  # available plain t-shirts\n    current_logo = 0   # available logo t-shirts (we haven't bought any yet)\n    \n    max_logo_needed = 0\n    current_worn = 0  # number of t-shirts currently worn and not washed\n    \n    # We need to simulate day by day\n    for i in range(N):\n        if S[i] == '0':\n            # No plans: wash all worn t-shirts\n            # All worn t-shirts become available from the next day\n            current_plain = min(plain_tshirts, current_plain + current_worn)\n            current_logo = min(logo_tshirts, current_logo + current_worn)\n            current_worn = 0\n        else:\n            # Has a plan\n            if S[i] == '2':\n                # Must wear logo t-shirt\n                if current_logo > 0:\n                    # Use an available logo t-shirt\n                    current_logo -= 1\n                else:\n                    # Need to use a logo t-shirt, but none available\n                    # This means we will need to buy more\n                    logo_tshirts += 1\n                    current_logo = max(0, current_logo + 1 - 1)  # use it immediately\n                current_worn += 1\n                max_logo_needed = max(max_logo_needed, logo_tshirts)\n            elif S[i] == '1':\n                # Can wear plain or logo\n                if current_plain > 0:\n                    # Prefer to use plain\n                    current_plain -= 1\n                elif current_logo > 0:\n                    # Use logo if no plain available\n                    current_logo -= 1\n                else:\n                    # Need to use a logo t-shirt (buy it)\n                    logo_tshirts += 1\n                    current_logo = max(0, current_logo + 1 - 1)  # use it immediately\n                current_worn += 1\n                max_logo_needed = max(max_logo_needed, logo_tshirts)\n    \n    # But the above simulation might overcount because we're buying one-by-one.\n    # Let's use a better approach: simulate with different numbers of purchased logo shirts\n    \n    def can_succeed(buy_logo):\n        avail_plain = M\n        avail_logo = buy_logo\n        worn = 0\n        \n        for i in range(N):\n            if S[i] == '0':\n                # Wash all\n                worn = 0\n                avail_plain = M\n                avail_logo = buy_logo\n            else:\n                if S[i] == '2':  # Need logo\n                    if avail_logo > 0:\n                        avail_logo -= 1\n                        worn += 1\n                    else:\n                        return False\n                else:  # S[i] == '1', can use plain or logo\n                    if avail_plain > 0:\n                        avail_plain -= 1\n                        worn += 1\n                    elif avail_logo > 0:\n                        avail_logo -= 1\n                        worn += 1\n                    else:\n                        return False\n        return True\n    \n    # Binary search or simply iterate since N <= 1000\n    for buy in range(0, N + 1):\n        if can_succeed(buy):\n            print(buy)\n            return\n    \n    print(N)  # fallback\n\nsolve()\n```",
