      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    it = iter(data)\n    N = int(next(it)); M = int(next(it))\n    \n    edges = []\n    \n    for _ in range(M):\n        K = int(next(it)); C = int(next(it))\n        verts = [int(next(it)) for _ in range(K)]\n        # Instead of adding all edges, use virtual node technique:\n        # Connect all vertices to a virtual node with weight C\n        # But since we need MST, better to use Kruskal on representative edges:\n        # For each operation, we can just record that all pairs have weight C,\n        # but that's too many edges. Instead, we can store just one edge per op: \n        # connect first vertex to all others with weight C (K-1 edges)\n        for i in range(1, K):\n            u, v = verts[0], verts[i]\n            edges.append((C, u, v))\n    \n    # Union-Find setup\n    parent = list(range(N+1))\n    rank = [0] * (N+1)\n    \n    def find(x):\n        if parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = find(parent[x])\n        return parent[x]\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return False\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\n        parent[ry] = rx\n        if rank[rx] == rank[ry]:\n            rank[rx] += 1\n        return True\n    \n    # Sort edges by weight\n    edges.sort()\n    \n    mst_weight = 0\n    count = 0\n    \n    for c, u, v in edges:\n        if union(u, v):\n            mst_weight += c\n            count += 1\n            if count == N-1:\n                break\n    \n    # Check connectivity: all vertices in same component?\n    root = find(1)\n    for i in range(2, N+1):\n        if find(i) != root:\n            print(-1)\n            return\n    \n    print(mst_weight)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
