    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    H, W = map(int, input().split())\n    grid = [input() for _ in range(H)]\n    \n    red_cells = []\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == '.':\n                red_cells.append((i, j))\n    \n    num_red_cells = len(red_cells)\n    \n    total_components = 0\n    for r, c in red_cells:\n        new_grid = [list(row) for row in grid]\n        new_grid[r][c] = '#'\n        \n        def count_components(grid):\n            visited = [[False] * W for _ in range(H)]\n            components = 0\n            \n            def dfs(i, j):\n                if i < 0 or i >= H or j < 0 or j >= W or visited[i][j] or grid[i][j] == '.':\n                    return\n                \n                visited[i][j] = True\n                dfs(i + 1, j)\n                dfs(i - 1, j)\n                dfs(i, j + 1)\n                dfs(i, j - 1)\n            \n            for i in range(H):\n                for j in range(W):\n                    if grid[i][j] == '#' and not visited[i][j]:\n                        components += 1\n                        dfs(i, j)\n            return components\n        \n        total_components += count_components(new_grid)\n    \n    \n    P = total_components\n    Q = num_red_cells\n    \n    def mod_inverse(a, m):\n        m0 = m\n        y = 0\n        x = 1\n        \n        if (m == 1):\n            return 0\n        \n        while (a > 1):\n            q = a // m\n            t = m\n            m = a % m\n            a = t\n            t = y\n            y = x - q * y\n            x = t\n        \n        if (x < 0):\n            x = x + m0\n            \n        return x\n\n    R = (P * mod_inverse(Q, 998244353)) % 998244353\n    print(R)\n\nsolve()\n```",
