tput 1\n\n3\r\n1 1 1 0 0 1 0 1\r\n\nThe sample output corresponds to the following actions:\n\n- Find potions of types 2,3,1 in this order. Pick up all of them.\n- Find potions of types 3,2 in this order. Do not pick up any of them.\n- Encounter a type-3 monster. Use one type-3 potion to defeat it.\n- Find a type-3 potion. Pick it up.\n- Find a type-3 potion. Do not pick it up.\n- Encounter a type-3 monster. Use one type-3 potion to defeat it.\n- Find a type-3 potion. Pick it up.\n- Encounter a type-2 monster. Use one type-2 potion to defeat it.\n- Encounter a type-3 monster. Use one type-3 potion to defeat it.\n- Encounter a type-1 monster. Use one type-1 potion to defeat it.\n\nIn this sequence of actions, the value of K is 3.\nThere is no way to avoid defeat with K\\leq 2, so the sought value of K _ {{\\min}} is 3.\r\nThere are multiple sequences of actions that satisfy K=3 and allow him to avoid defeat; you may print any of them.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n4\r\n2 3\r\n1 4\r\n2 1\r\n1 2\n\nSample Output 2\n\n-1\r\n\nHe will inevitably be defeated by the first monster he encounters.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n30\r\n1 25\r\n1 2\r\n1 10\r\n1 18\r\n2 18\r\n1 11\r\n2 11\r\n1 21\r\n1 6\r\n2 2\r\n2 10\r\n1 11\r\n1 24\r\n1 11\r\n1 3\r\n1 2\r\n1 18\r\n2 25\r\n1 8\r\n1 10\r\n1 11\r\n2 18\r\n2 10\r\n1 10\r\n2 2\r\n1 24\r\n1 10\r\n2 10\r\n1 25\r\n2 6\n\nSample Output 3\n\n4\r\n1 1 1 1 1 0 1 0 0 0 0 1 1 0 1 0 1 0 0 0",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    from collections import defaultdict\n    \n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    events = []\n    idx = 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        t = int(data[idx]); x = int(data[idx+1]); idx += 2\n        events.append((t, x))\n    \n    # First, check feasibility: need count of each type's potions >= count of monsters\n    potion_needed = defaultdict(int)\n    monster_count = defaultdict(int)\n    potion_events = []\n    \n    for i, (t, x) in enumerate(events):\n        if t == 1:\n            potion_needed[x] += 1\n            potion_events.append(i)\n        else:\n            monster_count[x] += 1\n    \n    # Check feasibility\n    for x in monster_count:\n        if potion_needed[x] < monster_count[x]:\n            print(-1)\n            return\n    \n    # Greedy strategy: Use online algorithm to minimize max inventory\n    # For each monster encounter, we need a potion available before that point\n    # Strategy: defer picking potions until needed, but ensure we have enough\n    \n    # Count how many of each potion type are used (exactly monster_count[x])\n    # Build required usage schedule\n    potions_used = defaultdict(int)\n    required_usage = defaultdict(list)\n    for i, (t, x) in enumerate(events):\n        if t == 2:\n            required_usage[x].append(i)\n    \n    # Assign required potions to monster events greedily\n    # For each monster event for type x, assign the earliest possible unassigned potion event before it\n    assigned_potions = [False] * len(potion_events)\n    monster_assignments = []\n    potion_idx_map = defaultdict(int)  # next available potion index for type x\n    \n    # Sort monster events by time\n    for x in sorted(required_usage.keys()):\n        monster_times = required_usage[x]\n        potion_times = [potion_events[i] for i in range(len(potion_events)) \n                       if events[potion_events[i]][1] == x]\n        \n        # Greedily match: for each monster (in order), find the earliest potion that hasn't been used yet\n        p_idx = 0\n        for m_time in monster_times:\n            while p_idx < len(potion_times) and potion_times[p_idx] <= m_time:\n                p_idx += 1\n            if p_idx == 0:\n                # Shouldn't happen if feasible\n                print(-1)\n                return\n            p_idx -= 1  # Now p_idx is the latest potion index <= m_time that we can use\n            # But we want earliest available, so iterate through potion_events and assign greedily\n            break\n        \n    # Better approach: simulate adventure, make decisions greedily\n    # Use a min-heap: when picking potions, we don't know which we'll need\n    # Alternate greedy: always hold potions, but drop potions when we have too many\n    # To minimize peak, use the following:\n    # - Only pick up a potion if we might need it\n    # - Specifically, for each type x, keep track how many more monsters left vs potions collected\n    # - Use a stack-like method\n    \n    # Simulate and make greedy choice: pick up only if we will need it\n    # For type x, keep count of remaining monsters after current time\n    # and potions picked so far. Only pick up if remaining monsters > current_potions\n    \n    from heapq import heappush, heappop\n    \n    # Precompute suffix monster counts per type\n    suffix_monsters = defaultdict(list)\n    temp_counts = defaultdict(int)\n    for i in range(n-1, -1, -1):\n        t, x = events[i]\n        if t == 2:\n            temp_counts[x] += 1\n        suffix_monsters[i] = dict(temp_counts)\n    \n    # Actually, better approach from known solution pattern:\n    # We simulate and for each potion event, decide whether to pick it based on future needs\n    \n    # Count how many monsters of each type remain at each event\n    monsters_remaining = defaultdict(int)\n    for t, x in events:\n        if t == 2:\n            monsters_remaining[x] += 1\n    \n    # Reset counters for simulation\n    inventory = defaultdict(int)\n    actions = []\n    current_max = 0\n    pick_actions = []\n    \n    for i, (t, x) in enumerate(events):\n        if t == 1:\n            # Decide whether to pick\n            # Check if we will need this potion\n            # How many monsters of type x remain? (including future)\n            need_x = monsters_remaining[x]\n            have_x = inventory[x]\n            # If have_x < need_x, we need at least one more potion\n            # But we also need to consider if picking now helps avoid needing more later\n            # Greedy: only pick if need_x > have_x\n            if have_x < need_x:\n                inventory[x] += 1\n                pick_actions.append(1)\n                current_max = max(current_max, sum(inventory.values()))\n            else:\n                pick_actions.append(0)\n        else:  # t == 2\n            # Must use a potion if available\n            if inventory[x] > 0:\n                inventory[x] -= 1\n            else:\n                print(-1)\n                return\n        # Update remaining monsters count\n        if t == 2:\n            monsters_remaining[x] -= 1\n    \n    print(current_max)\n    print(\" \".join(map(str, pick_actions)))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
