      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    L = list(map(int, data[2:2+n]))\n    \n    def can_fit(window_width):\n        lines_used = 1\n        current_line_width = 0\n        for i in range(n):\n            word_width = L[i]\n            if i == 0:\n                current_line_width = word_width\n            else:\n                # Try adding word with space\n                if current_line_width + 1 + word_width <= window_width:\n                    current_line_width += 1 + word_width\n                else:\n                    # Start new line\n                    lines_used += 1\n                    current_line_width = word_width\n            # Early termination if lines exceed m\n            if lines_used > m:\n                return False\n        return lines_used <= m\n    \n    # Binary search for minimum window width\n    left = max(L)  # Minimum possible width must be at least the longest word\n    right = sum(L) + n - 1  # Maximum possible width: all words in one line with spaces\n    result = right\n    \n    while left <= right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n        if can_fit(mid):\n            result = mid\n            right = mid - 1\n        else:\n            left = mid + 1\n    \n    print(result)\n\nsolve()\n```",
