      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findMaximumScore(nums, k):\n    n = len(nums)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Sort the array to group similar elements together\n    nums.sort()\n    \n    max_score = 1\n    \n    # Try to make each unique value the target value\n    for target in set(nums):\n        # Calculate cost to convert elements to target\n        cost = 0\n        count = 0\n        \n        for num in nums:\n            cost += abs(num - target)\n            if cost > k:\n                break\n            count += 1\n        \n        # If we can convert all elements to target within k operations\n        if cost <= k:\n            max_score = max(max_score, count)\n        else:\n            # Try to convert a subset of elements to target\n            # Use sliding window to find maximum number of elements we can convert\n            left = 0\n            current_cost = 0\n            \n            for right in range(n):\n                # Add the cost of converting nums[right] to target\n                current_cost += abs(nums[right] - target)\n                \n                # Shrink window from left if cost exceeds k\n                while current_cost > k and left <= right:\n                    current_cost -= abs(nums[left] - target)\n                    left += 1\n                \n                # Update max score with current window size\n                if current_cost <= k:\n                    max_score = max(max_score, right - left + 1)\n    \n    return max_score\n```",
